Recursion
Stack Trace — Recursive Call
int f(int a, int n) {
  if (n == 0) return 0;
  else if (*a % 2 == 0)
    return *a + f(a+1,n--);
  else
    return *a - f(a+1,n--);
}

int main() {
  int a[] = {2,7,1,3,4,1,1};
  printf("%d", f(a,11));
}
How recursion unwinds:
main → f(a,11) → f(a+1,10) → ... → f(a+n,0)
Each call waits on stack until base case returns 0.
Stack trace shown in notes:
main → a[2500] → f(0,150) → array {8,7,13,4,11,6} → results computed from right to left
Number of Steps to Reduce to Zero
int numberOfSteps(int num) {
  int count = 0;
  while (num != 0) {
    count++;
    if (num % 2 == 0)
      num = num / 2;
    else
      num = num - 1;
  }
  return count;
}
If even → divide by 2. If odd → subtract 1. Count total steps.
